      "type": "text",
      "text": "<p>In the pie: John Adams (Federalist), {expression/adams}; Thomas Jefferson (Democratic-Republican), {expression/jefferson}.</p><p>All electors' votes in 1800: {Votes1800}. Each elector cast two votes for president, so the votes add up to twice the number of electors.</p><p>Jefferson and Aaron Burr tied with 73 votes each, so the House of Representatives chose the president: Jefferson, on 17 February 1801. The 12th Amendment (1804) then gave electors separate votes for president and vice president.</p><p>{Note}</p><p><a href='https://www.archives.gov/electoral-college/1800' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Source: National Archives</a></p>"
